# No co-authors

Do not add anyone as a co-author. Commits and PRs must have a single author — the repository owner / whoever runs `git commit`.

- Do not add `Co-authored-by` trailers (Cursor, Copilot, other agents, or people).
- Do not pass `--trailer`, `git interpret-trailers`, or extra `-m` blocks that name co-authors.
- Do not put "Co-authored-by" in the PR body or commit message footer.

```text
# ❌ BAD
git commit -m "Fix encoding" -m "Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>"

# ✅ GOOD
git commit -m "Fix encoding"
```
